  m_Name: SpaceExploration
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  exhibitName: Space Exploration
  description: "Space Exploration is the investigation of outer space using advanced
    technology such as rockets, satellites, and telescopes. The term refers to activities
    beyond Earth\u2019s atmosphere, including studying planets, stars, and galaxies.
    It began in the mid-20th century and has led to major scientific discoveries.
    \n\nThe first artificial satellite, Sputnik 1, was launched by the Soviet Union
    in 1957. In 1961, Yuri Gagarin became the first human in space. The United States\u2019
    Apollo 11 mission landed astronauts on the Moon in 1969. Today, exploration includes
    the International Space Station, robotic missions to Mars, and telescopes like
    Hubble and James Webb. \n\nSpacecraft are designed to survive harsh conditions
    such as vacuum, radiation, and extreme temperatures. Missions aim to expand knowledge
    of the universe, search for extraterrestrial life, and develop technology for
    future interplanetary travel. Challenges include high costs, long durations,
    and health risks for astronauts. "
  images: []
